---
title: Blueberry muffins
servings: 12
yield: 12 muffins
tags: [american, vegetarian, quick]
cuisine: american
time: 38 minutes
source: Blueberry Muffins by King Arthur Baking, https://www.kingarthurbaking.com/recipes/blueberry-muffins-recipe
---

Heat the oven to 375°F (190°C). Line a #12-cup muffin pan{} with paper liners
and grease the liners.

Whisk the @all-purpose flour{2.25%cup}, @baking powder{1.5%tsp},
@baking soda{1/2%tsp} and @table salt{1/2%tsp} together.

In a #large bowl{}, beat the @unsalted butter{4%tbsp}(room temperature) with the
@granulated sugar{3/4%cup}, then beat in the @eggs{2} one at a time.

Beat in the @vanilla extract{2%tsp} and @sour cream{1/2%cup}, then the dry mix
on low speed until smooth. The batter is very thick.

Fold in the @blueberries{1.5%cup}(fresh or frozen) by hand.

Scoop a heaped quarter cup into each liner and sprinkle with
@coarse sparkling sugar{}(optional).

Bake ~{18%minutes} to 24 minutes, until a tester in the centre comes out clean.
Take them out of the pan as soon as you can and cool on a rack.

> Use 1/4 cup vegetable oil in place of the butter if you like, yogurt in place
> of the sour cream, and up to 7/8 cup sugar for tart berries.
